<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cambodia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cambodia is a country in mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>, the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire</a>, whose capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a> flourished between the ninth and fifteenth centuries. Its early art and religion were influenced by Indian traditions, including Gupta artistic conventions transmitted through trade and religious contact. Cambodia's temples and kingship reflected this blend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> and Buddhist influences.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cambodia.jpg" alt="Cambodia" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cambodia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
